# A worktree's own note about what it is for. It belongs to the feature
# DIRECTORY beside this checkout (CroftC/worktrees/<feature>/FEATURE.md), never
# inside it, and CroftC/.claude/COORDINATION.md § Feature workspaces says so in
# both its diagram and the word "untracked".
#
# Ignored rather than merely deleted, because deleting it alone does not hold:
# a tracked copy had landed on main SIX times before 2026-09-04 — quote posts,
# reply embeds, logged-out board, feed position, come-back-to-your-place, share
# to Forage — each landing overwriting the last, so main carried a rotating,
# always-stale description of whichever branch merged most recently, and every
# worktree cut from main inherited it.
#
# The rule already named the mechanism and lost to it anyway: sessions stage
# with `git add -A`, which is legal in a private worktree and is exactly how a
# file that should never be tracked gets swept in. This line is the part that
# does not depend on remembering.
FEATURE.md
